    {
      "form": "Sentence-final のです / のでした",
      "sources": [
        "https://bunpro.jp/grammar_points/-%E3%82%93%E3%81%A7%E3%81%99-%E3%81%AE%E3%81%A7%E3%81%99",
        "https://wasabi-jpn.com/magazine/japanese-grammar/explanatory-noda/"
      ],
      "formation": "Plain verb/i-adjective + のです; noun/na stem + なのです. Literary explanation distinguished from causal ので followed by a main clause.",
      "teachingChoice": "Narrator observation versus the visitors’ explanation. Overly absolute source register/gender restrictions are not adopted."
    },
    {
      "form": "Independent connector ところが",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.jpf.go.jp/j/project/japanese/teach/tsushin/grammar/201109.html",
        "https://bunpro.jp/grammar_points/ところが"
      ],
      "formation": "Expected or prior situation, followed by an established surprising result. Distinguish verb+たところが and topic-shifting ところで.",
      "teachingChoice": "Perfume expectation versus observed vinegar smell; no universal beyond-control rule."
    },
    {
      "form": "てください / お + masu stem + ください / ご + action noun + ください",
      "sources": [
        "https://bunpro.jp/grammar_points/お-ください",
        "https://www.tofugu.com/japanese-grammar/kudasai/"
      ],
      "formation": "塗ってください; 待つ→お待ちください; ご確認ください. Retrieve 塗る→塗れ in the quoted imperative.",
      "teachingChoice": "Politeness alone does not establish benevolent intent. Bunpro’s incompatible blanket restriction on ご is not adopted."
    },
    {
      "form": "食べさせる / 人を料理にする / 食べられる",
      "sources": [
        "https://bunpro.jp/grammar_points/causative",
        "https://bunpou.jepang.org/en/lesson/0143/saseru"
      ],
      "formation": "Xが人に料理を食べさせる versus Xが人を料理にする. 食べられる can be potential or passive, interpreted through context.",
      "teachingChoice": "Track eater and food rather than treating に as always permission and を as always force."
    }
  ],
